 ## Background
-The technique was popularized by Inigo Quilez, who described it as a way to obtain soft shadows with a penumbra region using distance fields by inspecting the distance $d$ from the ray to surrounding geometry and the traversal distance $t$ [S13, unofficial]. It is often referred to as "Quilez soft shadows" or "MIP shadow" in the demoscene and indie graphics communities [S1, S2, unofficial]. The method leverages the global geometric information provided by SDFs to approximate the visibility of an area light without the overhead of shadow maps or multiple ray samples [S12][S19, unofficial].
